# Hash-bound evidence repository: byte transparency is the only self-consistent
# default. `* -text` disables all newline translation (and overrides any
# core.autocrlf setting on contributor machines) so checked-out bytes equal
# committed bytes for everything not explicitly listed below.
* -text

# Textual contracts/evidence are written by LF-pinned writers and stored as LF
# blobs; pin checkout to LF so hash bindings survive on every machine.
*.json text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary evidence (png/pptx/…) falls through to the `* -text` default untouched.
# Historic note: cases 01-04 SVG blobs are already LF in the object database
# (verified by the renormalize audit), so the global LF pin does not rewrite them.
# 2026-08 regression lesson: requirements.txt was committed as a CRLF blob by the
# attributes migration itself (a `-text` passthrough `git add` on a CRLF-smudged
# worktree — changing attributes never re-cleans files already checked out).
# It is normalized back to LF and `*.txt` pinned above; tests/test_text_blob_eol.py
# now fails CI on any i/crlf or i/mixed text blob, closing the whole class.
